# EPAS clusters read by scripts/collect_all.sh.
# Copy to config/sources.conf on the central server (it is in .gitignore).
#
# One cluster per line, fields separated by spaces:
#   CODE   HOST   PORT   [DATABASE]   [USER]
#
# CODE      3-5 characters, A-Z and 0-9; use 4 or fewer (see README, "Source codes").
#           It becomes the ID prefix ("PRD1:app_read"). NEVER change a code once it is live:
#           SailPoint would see every account of that cluster as removed and re-added.
# DATABASE  optional; defaults to PGDATABASE in central.env (sailpoint).
# USER      optional; defaults to PGUSER in central.env.
#
# Each cluster needs the one-time setup (sql/setup), a pg_hba.conf line for the central
# server, and a ~/.pgpass line on the central server. A single cluster is simply one line.

# CODE   HOST                    PORT   DATABASE   USER
PRD1     pgprd01.example.com     5444
PRD2     pgprd02.example.com     5444
# UAT1   pguat01.example.com     5444   sailpoint  sailpoint_feed_uat
